      "text": "This problem asks for the distance between two points on a Cartesian plane. To solve this problem, we can use the distance formula:\n\nThe distance between two points \\(\\mathbf{P} = (x_1, y_1)\\) and \\(\\mathbf{Q} = (x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2} \\]\n\nHere, the coordinates of the given points are:\n\\(P = (-3, -4)\\) and\n\\(Q = (4, -5)\\).\n\nSubstituting these coordinates into the distance formula:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(4 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - (-4))^2} \\]\n\nSimplifying inside the parentheses:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{(4 + 3)^2 + (-5 + 4)^2} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{7^2 + (-1)^2} \\]\n\nCalculating the squares:\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{49 + 1} \\]\n\\[ d = \\sqrt{50} \\]\n\nThus the distance in simplest radical form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{50}}\n\\]",
